{
  "description": "Full vibrational Raman of LiH (HF, one rung: protocol 1e-4, k 6, l 50): alpha(0) xyz, the complete static polarizability gradient over all 3N = 6 nuclear coordinates (raman.nuc_atom -1; 54 rows under response_properties.raman), the Hessian assembled from the same six nuclear response states (vibrational_analysis), and the one vibrational mode with its Raman activity and depolarization ratio (raman_spectra). Asserted: the stretch frequency 1441.64 cm^-1 (rtol 0.01), d alpha_zz / d z_Li = -13.5346 and d alpha_zz / d z_H = +13.5086 (rows 50, 53; rtol 0.02; their sum is the translational-invariance residual, 0.2 %), activity 350.43 A^4/amu (rtol 0.02), depolarization ratio 0.0328 (rtol 0.05). For reading, not asserted: the removed molresponse_v2 engine gave 1427.94 cm^-1, 350.59 A^4/amu, 0.0323 and d alpha_zz/d z_Li = -13.502 at protocol [1e-4, 1e-5], l 80 (archived LiH reference), and the v3 single-component scripted test gives -13.549 at 1e-6/k8. Response dconv 1e-3 because the nuclear legs' responses are ~1e3 larger than a dipole leg's and the FD gate is absolute (see response_h2o_raman_tpa); nothing here is a converged Raman value. Reference: RelWithDebInfo, Pthreads, ArmPL, 1 rank x 10 threads, dd (Neoverse-N1), 2026-10-15, branch molresponse/full-raman on 0b4be47ec, wall 257 s (first run, cold).",
